==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|be|sot|lang=en}}. Compare to {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|assoten||lang=enm}}, {{term|assotten||to act foolishly; fall madly in love, become infatuated|lang=enm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒt|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|besots|besotting|besotted|besotted|past_ptc2=besotten}}

# To [[muddle]], [[stupefy]], or act [[foolishly]]; as with [[alcoholic]] [[liquor]] or [[infatuation]].
#: ''You expect me and my men '''to besot''' ourselves with your drugs, ...'' &mdash; Robert Sheckley, "Legend of Conquistadors", Fantasy & Science Fiction: Vol. 104, Iss. 4; pg. 50; Apr, 2003

